<metadata><name>Safe Harbor Race Weekend 2026 navigation courses</name><desc>2026 Safe Harbor Race Weekend (Aug 7-9, 2026), fixed-mark courses only. Sources: SI Div 1-2-3 (final); Exhibit 1 Around Prudence Island with Amendment 1 applied (marks 16 and 17 are yellow/orange set marks); Notice 3 (Friday custom courses 99 LONG / 99 SHORT); Exhibit 2 Div 3 Navigation Courses with Notices 7 and 9 (intended coastal courses Sat Aug 8 and Sun Aug 9, Area E); Exhibit 5 South Bay Race Chart (mark letters and the printed positions of marks 16, 17, N2); Div 4 SI with Exhibit 7 (courses # 1-21) and Exhibit 8 (marks A-I, printed approximate positions). Prudence Island race: rendezvous Area A (approx 0.5 NM SSW of Halfway Rock); finishing line in the vicinity of Fort Adams approx 0.4 NM N of Mark 2, between a blue flag on an RC boat and a nearby mark; Patience Island is also a mark (same side as R8) and is drawn by the track passing W of it. Div 3 coastal: Area E (W of Rose Island near R2 off Jamestown Harbor) for both ends; government marks have no required side unless designated rounding marks. Div 4: RC line within ~1 NM of Kettle Bottom Reef Gong 7 (or 2-3 NM SSW of it, as broadcast); distances assume the Castle Hill finishing line (Castle Hill Light to a buoy WNW of it); other finishing options are Fort Adams and the starting area. All boats pass under the Newport Pell Bridge through the centre span. Keep out of the Navy security zone off Coddington Cove / Coasters Harbor. All approximate points are placeholders - the RC broadcasts actual positions. Points named (routing) are not marks. Windward/leeward courses and marks without a printed position (Mark 1, J, K, custom courses) are not included.</desc></metadata>
